{%- comment -%}
  fye-buybox-eternity — the choices for rings whose variants are
  Metal x Diamond Quality: eternity, diamond and gem-set wedding rings.

  Built 31/08/2026. Rendered by main-product when the product is NOT a plain
  band. The plain branch lives inline in the section; this one is a snippet
  because three more types will follow the same shape and the section should
  not grow a fifth copy of a buy box.

  ── WHY THIS IS A DIFFERENT BUY BOX ───────────────────────────────────────

  Plain bands: one product per metal, variants are ring sizes.
  These:       one product per design, variants are Metal x Diamond Quality.

      Metal            Platinum, 18k Gold, 14k Gold, 9k Gold, Palladium
      Diamond Quality  D/E VVS, F/G VS, G Si, H Si, Lab-grown D VVS

  Both are VARIANT options and change the price. Two things that do NOT change
  the price are line-item properties instead:

      Gold colour   yellow / white / rose — same metal, same cost
      Ring size     no variant, so no price ladder

  which is why the OVERSIZE SURCHARGE exists here and not on plain bands. A
  size above the threshold sets `_size_surcharge: "Yes"` and the Oversize Ring
  Surcharge cart-transform function adds 10%. On plain rings the metal cost is
  already in the variant ladder, so applying it there would charge twice —
  Ed, 31/08/2026.

  ── METAL IS A LINK, NOT A RADIO ──────────────────────────────────────────

  Each metal is a link to ?variant=<id>, resolved in Liquid by finding the
  variant pairing that metal with the CURRENT quality. Three things follow:

    · the gold-colour row's presence is decided server-side on load, so no JS
      has to know that platinum has no colour;
    · a metal with no variant at the current quality is disabled rather than
      offered and then failing;
    · it matches the plain branch, where metal is also navigation.

  Quality stays a <select> because it changes only the price, which fye-ui.js
  already updates.

  ── PROPERTY NAMES ARE A CONTRACT ─────────────────────────────────────────

  Verbatim from live's product-block.js, because the workshop reads these off
  the order:

      "Gold colour"      value with " gold" stripped — "Yellow", not "Yellow Gold"
      "Ring size"
      "Engraving", "Engraving font"
      "_size_surcharge"  "Yes" — the underscore hides it from the customer

  Do not re-word any of them without checking what reads the order.

  Parameters: product, settings (the section's), current (chosen variant)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign p = product

  assign metal_opt = nil
  assign quality_opt = nil
  for option in p.options_with_values
    if option.name == 'Metal'
      assign metal_opt = option
    elsif option.name contains 'Quality'
      assign quality_opt = option
    endif
  endfor

  assign metal_now = metal_opt.selected_value
  assign quality_now = quality_opt.selected_value
  assign is_gold = false
  if metal_now contains 'Gold'
    assign is_gold = true
  endif

  assign golds = s.gold_colours | default: 'Yellow,White,Rose' | split: ','
  assign sizes = s.ring_sizes | default: 'A,A.5,B,B.5,C,C.5,D,D.5,E,E.5,F,F.5,G,G.5,H,H.5,I,I.5,J,J.5,K,K.5,L,L.5,M,M.5,N,N.5,O,O.5,P,P.5,Q,Q.5,R,R.5,S,S.5,T,T.5,U,U.5,V,V.5,W,W.5,X,X.5,Y,Y.5,Z,Z.5,Z+1,Z+1.5,Z+2,Z+2.5,Z+3,Z+3.5,Z+4,Z+4.5,Z+5,Z+5.5,Z+6,Z+6.5,Z+7,Z+7.5,Z+8,Z+8.5,Z+9,Z+9.5' | split: ','
  assign threshold = s.surcharge_size | default: 'Q'
-%}

{%- if metal_opt != nil -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <p class="pdp__label pdp__label--inline">Metal: <span class="pdp__labelval">{{ metal_now }}</span></p>
    <ul class="pdp__carats">
      {%- for value in metal_opt.values -%}
        {%- liquid
          comment
            This metal at the quality already chosen, so switching metal does
            not silently reset the diamond grade.
          endcomment
          assign target = nil
          for v in p.variants
            if v.option1 == value and v.option2 == quality_now
              assign target = v
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        <li>
          {%- if value == metal_now -%}
            <span class="pdp__carat is-current" aria-current="true">{{ value }}</span>
          {%- elsif target != nil -%}
            <a class="pdp__carat" href="{{ p.url }}?variant={{ target.id }}">{{ value }}</a>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="pdp__carat is-off">{{ value }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Gold colour: a property, not a variant, and only meaningful on a gold. On
  platinum and palladium the control is absent entirely rather than greyed — a
  disabled row would imply we might make a rose platinum.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if is_gold -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <p class="pdp__label pdp__label--inline">Gold colour</p>
    <ul class="pdp__colours">
      {%- for colour in golds -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign name = colour | strip
          assign tone = name | downcase | prepend: '--metal-18-'
        -%}
        <li>
          <label class="pdp__colour{% if forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
            <input class="visually-hidden"
                   type="radio"
                   name="properties[Gold colour]"
                   value="{{ name | escape }}"
                   data-fye-gold
                   {% if forloop.first %}checked{% endif %}>
            <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
            <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ name }}</span>
          </label>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if quality_opt != nil -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-quality">
      {{ quality_opt.name }}
      {%- if s.quality_help_url != blank -%}
        <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.quality_help_url }}">What do these mean?</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </label>
    <select class="pdp__select" id="pdp-quality" name="options[{{ quality_opt.name | escape }}]" data-fye-option>
      {%- for value in quality_opt.values -%}
        <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if quality_now == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The variant matcher in fye-ui.js joins every [data-fye-option] control to
  build a variant title. Metal is a link here, not a control, so its value
  reaches that join through this hidden input, which sits FIRST to match
  Shopify's "Metal / Quality" title order.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if metal_opt != nil -%}
  <input type="hidden" value="{{ metal_now | escape }}" data-fye-option>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if sizes.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-size">
      Ring size
      {%- if s.size_guide_url != blank -%}
        <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.size_guide_url }}">Find my size</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </label>
    <select class="pdp__select"
            id="pdp-size"
            name="properties[Ring size]"
            data-fye-size
            data-threshold="{{ threshold }}"
            required>
      <option value="">Select your size</option>
      {%- for size in sizes -%}
        <option>{{ size | strip }}</option>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>

    {%- comment -%}
      Enabled by fye-ui.js when the chosen size is above the threshold; the
      cart transform reads it. Disabled otherwise, and a disabled field is not
      posted, so an ordinary size carries no flag at all.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="properties[_size_surcharge]" value="Yes" data-fye-surcharge disabled>

    <p class="pdp__hint fine" data-fye-surcharge-note hidden>
      {{ s.surcharge_note | default: 'Sizes above Q use more metal, so a 10% surcharge applies. It is shown in the cart.' }}
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
